WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.100
Every tumour starts from
the body's own cells,

2
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.040
dividing when they shouldn't.

3
00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:08.020
Some of the genes in
those cells have changed.

4
00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:11.390
Usually it takes several
changes, not just one.

5
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.750
So speed isn't the whole story.

6
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.780
What matters is whether
division is still under control.

7
00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:23.330
Then how does one of the body's own,
normal genes turn into a cancer gene?

8
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:27.070
In this mission, you'll meet two
kinds of gene that control division,

9
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.690
and see what a mutation does to each.

10
00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:33.570
Then you'll find out why one mutated
copy can be enough for one kind,

11
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.570
but not for the other.

12
00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:40.120
Your mission: explain how a normal
gene turns into a cancer gene.
